    "created_at": "2025-10-01T08:32:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-01T08:32:39Z",
    "body": "> I think you can count WebKit as supportive of what appears to be a bug fix, but having more clarity on the state of implementations and what trade-off is being made, if any, would help.\r\n\r\n- Chrome doesn't implement these document active checks and so avoids the issue.\r\n- Firefox does. It has an additional assert to ensure that non-open dialogs don't appear in the document's \"open dialogs list\". We're failing that assert right now because it's possible for a non-open dialog to be in this list if the document becomes inactive during teardown.\r\n- WebKit hasn't implemented light dismiss so avoids this issue currently.\r\n\r\nI think the trade-off for implementing this fix:\r\n\r\n - On the plus side, there's less opportunity for non-open dialogs to appear in the open dialogs list.\r\n - I suppose that there is a potential for more errors, I could imagine someone being able to conjure up a test which gets into \"yet another weird state\". Try as I might, I cannot. ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
